NNOOTTEESS
       As  many  other implementations don’t support IIPPPPRROOTTOO__IICCMMPP raw sockets,
       this feature should not be relied on in portable programs.

       IICCMMPP__RREEDDIIRREECCTT packets are not sent  when  Linux  is  not  acting  as  a
       router.   They  are  also accepted only from the old gateway defined in
       the routing table and the redirect routes are expired after some time.

       The 64‐bit timestamp returned  by  IICCMMPP__TTIIMMEESSTTAAMMPP  is  in  milliseconds
       since the Epoch, 1970‐01‐01 00:00:00 +0000 (UTC).

       Linux ICMP internally uses a raw socket to send ICMPs.  This raw socket
       may appear in nneettssttaatt(8) output with a zero inode.

